{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788163007,"nonce":"idTgexQ16zHbB2MAtzxec5kiU3s=","message":"Fixed on `docs/ci-simplification` (da8b3e3). Not by lowering the baseline — by tests.\n\nThe 1.9pp drop was two `Ok(None)` evidence-port stubs landing untested:\n`infra_condition` (13de34f, ADR-0068) and `workspace_provisioning` (a8ade2e).\nGoing after them surfaced the real gap: the crate had never tested its three\nlaunch rejections either (clone/ADR-0045, build/ADR-0018, sidecar services/\nADR-0058) — the guards whose whole job is to refuse rather than run a step\nwithout the thing that makes it that kind of step. An unguarded clone step\nexits 0 having checked nothing out.\n\nFive tests added. Re-measured under full CI env parity (Postgres + MinIO, both\nREQUIRE flags): 64/83 -\u003e 75/83 lines, 77.1% -\u003e 90.4%, against an UNCHANGED\nbaseline of 80.0.\n\nTwo adjacent findings, fixed in d44af9b:\n- `just coverage` never started MinIO or set SCARAB_TEST_S3_* despite claiming\n  to mirror the CI job — and it is the recipe that WRITES this baseline. The\n  committed floors are 1-16pp low across most crates (scarab-storage-s3 +15.7,\n  scarab-secrets-postgres +14.2), which is the shape of a floor written without\n  MinIO. Deliberately NOT regenerated from a laptop run; see the note now in\n  coverage-baseline.toml.\n- the lcov artifact was uploaded only on GREEN runs (the step sat after the\n  ratchet step that fails), which is why this ticket had to be reconstructed by\n  reading percentages out of four job logs. `if: always()` now (bd6eaea).","files":null}]}